firedamp
========

Methane plume aggregator. It maps satellite plume detections with candidate
oil and gas infrastructure and shows source attributions produced offline by
the ch4id repository.

Live: https://research.datadesk.eco/firedamp/


Data
----

Public plumes come directly from these provider objects in the CloudFerro
archive:

- `carbon-mapper/detections/data.parquet`
- `imeo/detections/data.parquet`
- `sron/detections/data.parquet`
- `data-desk/detections/data.parquet`

A detections table also holds flares, so the browser reads the four objects
with `kind = 'plume'`. The private map also contains licensed GHGSat rows and
MapStand licence polygons.

Candidate infrastructure remains provider-owned. DuckDB-Wasm queries four
Hilbert-sorted GeoParquet files by viewport:

- `mapstand/infrastructure/data.parquet`
- `ogim/infrastructure/data.parquet`
- `osm/infrastructure/data.parquet`
- `gem/infrastructure/data.parquet`

Attributions use `data-desk/attributions/data.parquet`. The browser does not run
an attribution model.


Repository layout
-----------------

```
web/                    static ES-module application
  config.js             sources, layers, filters, key, table, and detail panel
  attribution.js        attribution rendering and wind statistic
  candidates.js         provider GeoParquet viewport queries
  licences.js           private MapStand GeoParquet viewport queries
  vendor/               Cartograph, DuckDB-Wasm, MapLibre, design assets, fonts
scripts/
  dist.sh               Pages artifact
  serve.py              development server
  vendor.sh             shared dependency copy
```

The ETL repository retrieves and publishes the source tables. Firedamp reads
them and does not maintain a second plume or feature aggregation.


Development
-----------

```
make vendor
make serve
```

The local server runs on port 8000. A local `web/data/plumes.parquet` overrides
the public plume tables. The private deployment also expects
`web/data/licences.parquet`.


Deployment
----------

Pushing `main` deploys the public GitHub Pages site. It reads the provider
tables live from:

```
https://s3.WAW3-2.cloudferro.com/data-desk-archive
```

`make deploy-private` builds the licensed plume and licence files, checks the
Cloudflare Access gate, and deploys `firedamp-private`. Public and private builds
use `scripts/dist.sh`; add new browser assets there.


